{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>Dwell in the land which, etc.</b> It intends to say, simply, to bind himself to accept the holy words of HaShem toward the place that He would tell him — even if it be contrary to his desire — and to receive reward for this thing, for HaShem wished to merit His beloved. And so He says (Genesis 12:1): ״אֶל הָאָרֶץ אֲשֶׁר אַרְאֶךָּ״, and shortly after He made it known to him, as it is written (Genesis 12:5): ״לָלֶכֶת אַרְצָה כְּנָעַן״."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:43:24.606259546Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}